      "writtenOn": "2026-02-24T16:37:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If my understanding is correct, `requiresBarrier` means that self intersection is no longer allowed. \n\nSo, we only make the `requiresBarrier` check if we would have been able to self intersect. Stencils may never self intersect so we only make this check on the singleDraw path.\n\n\nRegardless of the list type, except in the case of compatibly overlapping singleDraws, we always check for intersection. The type of the list does not affect this except as a convenient quick reject for matching. i.e. Single draws should not match with stencils, and vice versa.",
